</div>

<div class="section">

  <h2>Step-by-Step Installation Guide</h2>

  <h3>A. On Android Using ZArchiver & PPSSPP</h3>

  <ol>

    <li><strong>Install ZArchiver:</strong> Download from Google Play Store and grant storage permissions.</li>

    <li><strong>Download PPSSPP:</strong> Obtain the latest PPSSPP Gold or free build from the Play Store.</li>

    <li><strong>Download ISO File:</strong> Save the God of War PSP ISO to your device''s download folder. If compressed (ZIP/7Z), proceed to next step.</li>

    <li><strong>Extract with ZArchiver:</strong> Open ZArchiver, locate the downloaded archive, and choose <em>Extract here</em>. This will produce the ISO file.</li>

    <li><strong>Launch PPSSPP Emulator:</strong> Open PPSSPP, tap <em>Games</em>, and navigate to the folder containing the ISO.</li>

    <li><strong>Select ISO & Configure:</strong> Tap the ISO to launch. Under <em>Settings → Graphics</em>, enable <em>Backface Culling</em> and set rendering resolution to 2x for improved visuals.</li>

    <li><strong>Customize Controls:</strong> In <em>Settings → Controls Mapping</em>, assign on-screen buttons as you prefer. Consider using a Bluetooth controller for precision.</li>

    <li><strong>Play & Save Progress:</strong> Use save states (<em>Quick Save → Slot 1</em>) for instant checkpoints without relying only on in-game saves.</li>

  </ol>

  <h3>B. On PC Using PPSSPP</h3>

  <ol>

    <li><strong>Download PPSSPP for Windows:</strong> Visit the official PPSSPP website and get the latest Windows build.</li>

    <li><strong>Extract ISO (if needed):</strong> Use software like 7-Zip to extract compressed archives.</li>

    <li><strong>Install & Run PPSSPP:</strong> Launch PPSSPP.exe.

      <ul>

        <li>Go to <em>File → Open</em> and select the God of War ISO.</li>

      </ul>

    </li>

    <li><strong>Configure Graphics:</strong>

      <ul>

        <li>Set <em>Rendering Resolution</em> to <code>3x PSP</code> for high-definition output.</li>

        <li>Enable <em>Hardware Transform</em> and <em>Threaded Rendering</em> for performance.</li>

      </ul>

    </li>

    <li><strong>Control Setup:</strong> In <em>Settings → Controls → Control Mapping</em>, assign keys or connect a gamepad for best experience.</li>

    <li><strong>Performance Tweaks:</strong> Under <em>Settings → System</em>, enable <em>I/O on thread</em> to reduce stutters.

    </li>

    <li><strong>Start Playing:</strong> Use quick saves via <em>Emulation → Save State → Slot 1</em> to preserve progress anytime.</li>

  </ol>

