<p>

Did you know that your Android phone has <strong>hidden dial codes</strong> that unlock powerful menus, test hardware, reveal system information, and even fix common issues?

</p>

<p>

These secret Android codes work directly from the phone dialer and are used by technicians, developers, and advanced users. Most Android users never discover them, yet they can help you diagnose problems, check phone authenticity, improve performance, and understand your device deeply.

</p>

<div class="note">

<strong>Important:</strong> Not all codes work on every phone. Availability depends on brand, Android version, and carrier.

</div>

---

<h2>What Are Secret Android Codes?</h2>

<p>

Secret Android codes (also called <strong>USSD codes</strong> or <strong>dialer codes</strong>) are special combinations of numbers and symbols entered using the phone dialer.

</p>

<p>

Unlike normal phone numbers, these codes instantly trigger hidden system actions without making a call. Manufacturers use them for testing, troubleshooting, and quality control.

</p>

---

<h2>How to Use Android Secret Codes</h2>

<ol>

<li>Open your phone’s <strong>Dialer</strong></li>

<li>Enter the code exactly as shown</li>

<li>No need to press call – it executes automatically</li>

</ol>

<div class="warning">

<strong>Warning:</strong> Do NOT use reset or erase codes unless you understand them fully.

</div>

---

<h2>Most Popular Android Secret Codes</h2>

<table>

<tr>

<th>Code</th>

<th>Function</th>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>*#06#</td>

<td>Check IMEI number</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>*#*#4636#*#*</td>

<td>Phone information & usage stats</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>*#*#7780#*#*</td>

<td>Factory data reset (soft)</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>*#*#34971539#*#*</td>

<td>Camera information</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>*#*#2664#*#*</td>

<td>Touch screen test</td>

</tr>

</table>

---

<h2>Android Hardware Testing Codes</h2>

<h3>Touch Screen Test</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#2664#*#*</p>

<p>Test your touchscreen accuracy and responsiveness.</p>

<h3>Display Test</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#0*#*#*</p>

<p>Checks screen colors, brightness, dead pixels, and display issues.</p>

<h3>Vibration & Sensor Test</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#0842#*#*</p>

<p>Tests vibration motor and sensor response.</p>

---

<h2>Battery & Performance Codes</h2>

<h3>Battery Status</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#4636#*#*</p>

<p>

Shows battery health, charging status, voltage, temperature, and usage statistics.

</p>

<h3>Usage Statistics</h3>

<p>

This hidden menu also reveals how long apps have been running, helping you identify battery drainers.

</p>

---

<h2>Network & Connectivity Codes</h2>

<h3>Network Information</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#4636#*#*</p>

<p>View signal strength, network type (LTE, 5G), and connection details.</p>

<h3>Wi-Fi MAC Address</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#232338#*#*</p>

<p>Displays your device’s Wi-Fi MAC address.</p>

<h3>Bluetooth Address</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#232337#*#*</p>

<p>Check Bluetooth hardware address.</p>

---

<h2>Camera Secret Codes</h2>

<h3>Camera Firmware Info</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#34971539#*#*</p>

<p>

Displays camera firmware version, update count, and technical details.

</p>

<h3>Advanced Camera Testing</h3>

<p>

Useful when diagnosing camera crashes, focus problems, or blurry images.

</p>

---

<h2>System & Software Information Codes</h2>

<h3>Software Version</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#1234#*#*</p>

<p>Displays firmware version details.</p>

<h3>Build & PDA Information</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#1111#*#*</p>

<p>Shows system build data.</p>

---

<h2>Android Reset & Recovery Codes (Use Carefully)</h2>

<div class="warning">

These codes can erase data. Use only if necessary.

</div>

<h3>Soft Reset</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *#*#7780#*#*</p>

<p>Resets system settings without deleting files.</p>

<h3>Hard Factory Reset</h3>

<p><strong>Code:</strong> *2767*3855#</p>

<p>Completely wipes device and reinstalls firmware.</p>

---

<h2>Brand-Specific Android Codes</h2>

<h3>Samsung Secret Codes</h3>

<ul>

<li>*#0*# – Full hardware test menu</li>

<li>*#0228# – Battery status</li>

<li>*#0808# – USB configuration</li>

</ul>

<h3>Xiaomi (MIUI) Codes</h3>

<ul>

<li>*#*#6484#*#* – Hardware test menu</li>

<li>*#*#4636#*#* – Phone info</li>

</ul>

<h3>Huawei Codes</h3>

<ul>

<li>*#*#2846579#*#* – Project menu</li>

</ul>

---

<h2>Why Secret Android Codes Are Useful</h2>

<ul>

<li>Diagnose hardware problems</li>

<li>Check phone authenticity</li>

<li>Fix network and battery issues</li>

<li>Improve device performance</li>

<li>Learn advanced Android features</li>

</ul>

---

<h2>Safety Tips When Using Android Codes</h2>

<ul>

<li>Never experiment with unknown reset codes</li>

<li>Avoid firmware update menus unless instructed</li>

<li>Backup data before advanced actions</li>

<li>Codes may not work on all devices</li>

</ul>

---

<h2>Final Thoughts</h2>

<p>

Secret Android codes are powerful tools hidden inside your phone. When used correctly, they can help you troubleshoot issues, test hardware, and understand your device like a pro.

</p>

<p>

