<main class="wrap">

  <section class="grid">

    <article class="card col-8">

      <h2>Overview</h2>

      <p>

        WhatsApp keeps rolling out quiet updates—features that don’t always make headlines but radically improve

        how you chat, share, and protect your privacy. In this colorful 2025 guide, we’ll break down ten hidden (or

        easily overlooked) features and show you exactly how to enable them. Whether you’re a casual chatter,

        a group admin, or a creator building an audience with Channels, these tips will help you chat smarter.

      </p>

      <div class="note">

        Availability may vary by region, device, or app version. If you don’t see an option yet, update WhatsApp from Google Play/App Store and check again.

      </div>

    </article>

    <aside class="card col-4">

      <h2>Quick Labels</h2>

      <div class="labels">

        <span class="pill">WhatsApp Tips 2025</span>

        <span class="pill">Hidden Features</span>

        <span class="pill">Chat Lock</span>

        <span class="pill">HD Photos</span>

        <span class="pill">Status Tricks</span>

        <span class="pill">Channels</span>

        <span class="pill">Privacy</span>

      </div>

    </aside>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n1">1</span> Lock Individual Chats (Plus Secret Code)</h3>

    <p>

      You can lock specific conversations behind your fingerprint/Face ID and even hide the locked chat folder behind a secret code. 

      Perfect for separating personal and work life or protecting sensitive threads from shoulder surfers.

    </p>

    <div class="step">

      <strong>How to:</strong>

      Open a chat → tap the contact/group name → <em>Chat lock</em> → <em>Lock this chat</em>.  

      Then go to <em>Settings → Privacy → Chat lock</em> to set a <em>Secret code</em> (e.g., <span class="pill">#recipes</span>). 

      Type your secret code in the search bar to reveal the hidden folder.

    </div>

    <div class="tip"><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Use a neutral secret code that isn’t obviously personal.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n2">2</span> Passkeys & Device Unlock Integration</h3>

    <p>

      Passkeys let you sign in on a new phone using the same secure method you use to unlock your device (fingerprint, Face ID, or PIN), 

      reducing reliance on SMS codes. This speeds up login and defends against SIM-swap risks.

    </p>

    <div class="step"><strong>How to:</strong> Settings → Account → Passkeys (if available) → Set up. Follow your device prompts.</div>

    <div class="tip"><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Enable a screen lock with biometric auth for stronger overall protection.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n3">3</span> Send HD Photos & Videos (Toggle + Default)</h3>

    <p>

      WhatsApp compresses media by default, but you can send higher quality photos/videos. 

      Some devices also offer a preference to default to HD quality so you don’t need to toggle each time.

    </p>

    <div class="step">

      <strong>How to:</strong> Attach photo/video → tap the <em>HD</em> icon → choose <em>HD</em> → send.  

      Check <em>Settings → Storage and data → Media upload quality</em> for default preferences if available.

    </div>

    <div class="tip"><strong>Pro tip:</strong> For documents (e.g., PDFs/images as files), use the <em>Document</em> option to avoid image compression entirely.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n1">4</span> Edit Sent Messages (Within Time Limit)</h3>

    <p>

      Made a typo or sent the wrong figure? You can edit a message shortly after sending. An “Edited” label keeps conversations transparent.

    </p>

    <div class="step"><strong>How to:</strong> Long-press your message → <em>Edit</em> → fix → confirm.</div>

    <div class="warn"><strong>Note:</strong> Edits are time-limited and visible to all chat members.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n2">5</span> View Once: Photos/Videos That Don’t Stick Around</h3>

    <p>

      Send sensitive media that can be viewed only once. Perfect for passwords, IDs, or confidential whiteboards—just remind recipients not to screenshot.

    </p>

    <div class="step"><strong>How to:</strong> Attach photo/video → tap the “1” icon → send.</div>

    <div class="tip"><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Combine with chat lock for a privacy one-two punch.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n3">6</span> Disappearing Messages + Keep in Chat</h3>

    <p>

      Turn on disappearing messages to auto-clean chats. If someone posts a critical detail (like a receipt), you can pin it with “Keep in Chat,” 

      which flags the original sender—they can unkeep it if they want to maintain privacy.

    </p>

    <div class="step"><strong>How to:</strong> Chat → name → <em>Disappearing messages</em> → choose 24 hours/7 days/90 days.  

      Long-press any message → <em>Keep</em> to save it from auto-deletion.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n1">7</span> Channels for Broadcasts (No Numbers Revealed)</h3>

    <p>

      Channels let creators, businesses, or clubs broadcast updates to followers without exposing phone numbers. 

      Great for news, release notes, or event announcements—readers can react or forward, but only admins can post.

    </p>

    <div class="step"><strong>How to:</strong> Updates tab → “+” → <em>Create channel</em> → name, description, logo → share invite link.</div>

    <div class="tip"><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Post at consistent times and use concise titles for skimmability. Cross-promote via Status.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n2">8</span> Advanced Privacy: Silence Unknown Callers & Hidden Online Status</h3>

    <p>

      You can filter nuisance calls and hide your online presence while still chatting. Combine with read-receipts control to tailor your visibility.

    </p>

    <div class="step">

      <strong>How to:</strong> Settings → Privacy → <em>Last seen & online</em> (choose who can see) • <em>Read receipts</em> (toggle) • <em>Calls → Silence unknown callers</em>.

    </div>

    <div class="tip"><strong>Pro tip:</strong> In Groups → <em>Who can add me</em> set to Contacts or My contacts except… to block spam adds.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n3">9</span> Status Power-Ups: Voice Notes, Audience Control, and Link Previews</h3>

    <p>

      Beyond photos and 30-sec videos, you can post voice statuses, choose a custom audience per post, and share links with rich previews to drive clicks.

    </p>

    <div class="step"><strong>How to:</strong> Status/Updates → New status → tap mic for voice, or choose media → audience selector (top) → share.</div>

    <div class="tip"><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Use short captions with an emoji or two. Long blocks reduce completion rates.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card feature">

    <h3><span class="num n1">10</span> Proxy Mode When WhatsApp Is Blocked</h3>

    <p>

      If your network blocks WhatsApp, you can connect through a community proxy. You’ll still get end-to-end encryption when using a working proxy.

    </p>

    <div class="step">

      <strong>How to:</strong> Settings → Storage and data → Proxy → <em>Use proxy</em> → add proxy address/port → Save.  

      When connected, a banner shows you’re using a proxy.

    </div>

    <div class="warn"><strong>Note:</strong> Only use proxies you trust. If messages won’t send, switch to a different proxy or disable.</div>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card">

    <h2>Bonus Tricks to Level Up Your WhatsApp</h2>

    <ul>

      <li><strong>Star important messages:</strong> Long-press → ⭐ Star. View them via chat → name → Starred messages.</li>

      <li><strong>Search by date/person:</strong> In a chat, tap the name → Search → filter by keyword, sender, or date if available on your device.</li>

      <li><strong>Share in original quality:</strong> Use <em>Document</em> to send images/videos/files without compression.</li>

      <li><strong>Message yourself:</strong> Save ideas, files, and links in your personal chat. It syncs across devices.</li>

      <li><strong>Two-step verification:</strong> Settings → Account → Two-step verification → Enable PIN + email.</li>

      <li><strong>Companion mode:</strong> Link WhatsApp to a second phone: Settings → Linked devices → Link a device → scan QR.</li>

      <li><strong>Storage cleanup:</strong> Settings → Storage and data → Manage storage → sort by size to delete junk quickly.</li>

      <li><strong>Group controls:</strong> Only admins can post: Group → Settings → Send messages → Only admins.</li>

    </ul>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card">

    <h2>Troubleshooting Common Issues</h2>

    <h3>Feature not showing?</h3>

    <p>Update WhatsApp → restart phone → confirm region availability. Some features roll out gradually.</p>

    <h3>Phone doesn’t support biometrics?</h3>

    <p>Use a strong screen lock/PIN and enable two-step verification as a backup security layer.</p>

    <h3>HD media option missing?</h3>

    <p>Try sending via <em>Document</em> or check your app version. Also ensure you have enough storage.</p>

  </section>

  

  <section class="card">

    <h2>Safety & Privacy Reminders</h2>

    <ul>

      <li>Enable <strong>two-step verification</strong> and keep your email updated for recovery.</li>

      <li>Turn off <strong>read receipts</strong> and hide <strong>online status</strong> if you need quiet focus.</li>

      <li>Avoid unknown proxies or sketchy “mods” of WhatsApp that can leak data or get your number banned.</li>

      <li>Verify contacts claiming to be support or friends asking for codes. WhatsApp never asks for your 6-digit code in chat.</li>

    </ul>

  </section>

  

