      border-radius: 4px;}</style><div class="post-html"><p>Are you tired of seeing <strong>yourname.blogspot.com</strong> instead of your own clean domain name? Good news — you can <strong>remove “.blogspot.com”</strong> and use a custom domain like <strong>www.yoursite.com</strong> instead!</p>

  <p>Here’s the <strong>step-by-step guide</strong>, plus the <strong>best ways</strong> to do it for free or super cheap.</p>

  <h2>✅ Why remove “.blogspot.com”?</h2>

  <p>Having your own domain:</p>

  <ul>

    <li>Looks <strong>professional</strong> (great for sponsors and visitors!)</li>

    <li>Builds your <strong>brand</strong> — you fully own it</li>

    <li>Helps your site rank better in <strong>Google search</strong></li>

    <li>You can get a <strong>professional email</strong> later (like info@yoursite.com)</li>

  </ul>

  <h2>📌 1️⃣ The easiest way: Buy a .com domain</h2>

  <p>The best way to remove “.blogspot.com” is to buy your own <strong>.com</strong> domain.</p>

  <p><strong>Recommended:</strong></p>

  <p><a href="https://www.namecheap.com/" class="btn" target="_blank">Buy at Namecheap</a> — popular, cheap, and includes <strong>free WHOIS privacy</strong>.</p>

  <p>Most .com domains cost only <strong>$8–$12/year</strong>, that’s it!</p>

  <h2>✅ How to connect your .com to Blogger</h2>

  <ol>

    <li>Sign in to <a href="https://www.blogger.com" target="_blank">Blogger</a>.</li>

    <li>Go to <strong>Settings &gt; Publishing</strong> and click <strong>Custom Domain</strong>.</li>

    <li>Enter your new domain (like <strong>www.yoursite.com</strong>).</li>

    <li>Blogger shows you <strong>CNAME records</strong> — copy them!</li>

    <li>Log in to your domain registrar (e.g. Namecheap).</li>

    <li>Find <strong>DNS Management</strong> → add the <strong>CNAMEs</strong> that Blogger gave you.</li>

    <li>Add these <strong>A Records</strong> to Google’s IPs:

      <pre>

216.239.32.21

216.239.34.21

216.239.36.21

216.239.38.21

      </pre>

    </li>

    <li>Click <strong>Save</strong> in Blogger.</li>

    <li>Wait a few minutes or hours — your new domain will connect!</li>

    <li>🔒 Turn on <strong>HTTPS</strong> in Blogger’s settings.</li>

  </ol>

  <div class="note">

    ✅ Done! Now your site shows as <strong>www.yoursite.com</strong> — no more Blogspot!

  </div>

  <h2>📌 2️⃣ What if you want it 100% free?</h2>

  <p>👉 Use <a href="https://www.freenom.com" target="_blank">Freenom</a> — it gives you a free domain like:</p>

  <ul>

    <li>.tk</li>

    <li>.ml</li>

    <li>.ga</li>

    <li>.cf</li>

    <li>.gq</li>

  </ul>

  <p>It’s free for <strong>1 year</strong> and renewable — but:</p>

  <ul>

    <li>Many free extensions have a <strong>bad reputation</strong>.</li>

    <li>Some big sites block them.</li>

    <li>They’re not great for SEO.</li>

    <li>They can suspend your domain anytime.</li>

  </ul>

  <p>Still, it’s good for <strong>testing</strong> or a <strong>starter site</strong>.</p>

  <h2>✅ How to use Freenom with Blogger</h2>

  <ol>

    <li>Get a free domain at <a href="https://www.freenom.com" target="_blank">Freenom</a>.</li>

    <li>Follow the same steps:

      <ul>

        <li>Add your domain in Blogger’s <strong>Custom Domain</strong>.</li>

        <li>Copy the CNAMEs.</li>

        <li>Add them in Freenom’s DNS settings.</li>

      </ul>

    </li>

    <li>Save and wait!</li>

  </ol>

  <h2>✅ 3️⃣ Or get hosting + free domain</h2>

  <p>Some web hosts give you a <strong>free .com</strong> for the first year when you buy hosting.</p>

  <p>Good for WordPress too!</p>

  <p>👉 Examples:

    <a href="https://www.bluehost.com/" class="btn" target="_blank">Try Bluehost</a> |

    <a href="https://www.hostinger.com/" class="btn" target="_blank">Try Hostinger</a>

  </p>

  <h2>📌 💡 Final tip</h2>

  <p><strong>If you’re serious</strong> about your website, blog, or business — get a real <strong>.com</strong>. It’s only about <strong>$10/year</strong> at <a href="https://www.namecheap.com/" target="_blank">Namecheap</a>.</p>

  <p>You’ll look professional. It’s worth it for sponsors, SEO, and trust. Use <strong>Blogger</strong> for free hosting — easy!</p>

  <h2>✅ Ready to get started?</h2>

  <p>👉 <a href="https://www.namecheap.com/" class="btn" target="_blank">Get a domain at Namecheap</a>  

  👉 <a href="https://www.blogger.com" class="btn" target="_blank">Connect it to Blogger</a>  

  👉 Say goodbye to “.blogspot.com” forever!</p>

  <h2>⚡️ Need help?</h2>

  <p>If you want, I can:</p>

  <ul>

    <li>Help you pick the best domain name.</li>

    <li>Guide you step-by-step with DNS setup.</li>

    <li>Write a custom tutorial for <strong>Namecheap</strong>, <strong>Freenom</strong>, or <strong>Bluehost</strong>.</li>

  </ul>

  <p>💬 Just comment below or contact me anytime — and good luck with <strong>www.yoursite.com</strong>! 🚀</p></div>','published','2025-07-14T14:30:00.003Z',null,'🎮 How to Remove “.blogspot.com” From Your Blogger Site','How to Remove “.blogspot.com” and Use a Custom Domain','How to Remove “.blogspot.com” and Use a Custom Domain',array['tech']::text[],'ELIAH TECH',(select id from public.categories where slug='tech-tips-tutorials'),null,'guide',null,null,null,null,3,false,false,false) on conflict(slug) do nothing;
