    </p>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>🎮 Gameplay Overview</h2>

    <p>

      The gameplay in <strong>Crash of the Titans</strong> is a refreshing change from classic Crash platforming — it blends action with strategy by letting Crash <strong>control giant enemies called Titans</strong>. Instead of jumping through obstacles only, you:

    </p>

    <ul>

      <li>Battle hordes of mutant enemies</li>

      <li>Perform combo attacks and powerful strikes</li>

      <li>Possess Titans for massive damage</li>

      <li>Use special abilities unlocked by defeating enemies</li>

    </ul>

    <p>

      Combat feels smooth and energetic — every level is packed with action, diverse enemies, and colorful environments to explore. This all makes it perfect for handheld play on PSP or emulators.

    </p>

    <img class="game-img" src="https://via.placeholder.com/600x350.png?text=Crash+controlling+a+Titan" alt="Crash controlling a Titan" />

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>⚙️ How to Install and Play (Step-by-Step)</h2>

    <h3>📌 Requirements</h3>

    <ul>

      <li>A PSP Emulator (like PPSSPP)</li>

      <li>The downloaded .7z game file</li>

      <li>File extraction tool (ZArchiver, WinRAR, 7-Zip)</li>

    </ul>

    <h3>🔧 Installation Guide</h3>

    <ol>

      <li>Download the game using the Mediafire link above.</li>

      <li>Extract the .7z archive to get the ISO/CSO file.</li>

      <li>Open your PSP emulator (e.g., PPSSPP).</li>

      <li>Select ‘Load Game’ and navigate to the extracted file.</li>

      <li>Start playing Crash of the Titans!</li>

    </ol>

    <h3>🎮 Tips for Smooth Play</h3>

    <ul>

      <li>Set graphics to “Buffered Rendering” for better visuals.</li>

      <li>Use a controller on PC if possible for more responsive combat.</li>

      <li>Save your progress often to avoid replaying tough levels.</li>

    </ul>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>🧠 Tips & Tricks for Beginners</h2>

    <p>

      Whether you’re new to PSP games or a Crash fan, mastering this game takes strategy:

    </p>

    <ul>

      <li><strong>Control Titans wisely:</strong> Some Titans are strong but slow — use them to break shields and defeat groups.</li>

      <li><strong>Explore levels:</strong> Secret paths often hide health pickups and bonus items.</li>

      <li><strong>Use combos:</strong> Attack sequences unlock stronger abilities and score bonuses.</li>

      <li><strong>Save items:</strong> Don’t use health pickups unless necessary — save them for boss fights.</li>

    </ul>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>📊 Graphics and Sound</h2>

    <p>

      Despite being a PSP title, the visuals are outstanding — vibrant colors, detailed character models, and imaginative level design that brings the Crash universe to life. The sound design keeps the energy high with dynamic music and satisfying combat effects.

    </p>

    <img class="game-img" src="https://via.placeholder.com/600x350.png?text=Crash+of+the+Titans+Level+Screenshot" alt="Crash of the Titans level screenshot" />

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>💭 Final Thoughts — Is It Worth Playing?</h2>

    <p>

      Absolutely! <strong>Crash of the Titans PSP</strong> is one of the standout PSP action games. It’s fun, offers hours of combat, has replayability, and lets you experience Crash Bandicoot in a refreshed, exciting format. It’s perfect for both retro gamers and players who love action beat-’em-ups.

    </p>

    <p>

      Whether you’re trying it on your phone with PPSSPP or on your PC, this version brings a nostalgic yet fresh experience.

