  <h2>🎮 Can You Play PSP Games Online?</h2>

  <p>Yes, you can! Even though Sony shut down official PSP servers, you can still play multiplayer games online using the <strong>PPSSPP emulator</strong> and a virtual LAN tool like <strong>ZeroTier</strong>.</p>

  <h2>🧰 What You''ll Need</h2>

  <ul>

    <li>📲 PPSSPP Emulator</li>

    <li>🕹️ PSP game that supports Adhoc Multiplayer (e.g., Tekken 6, Monster Hunter)</li>

    <li>🌐 Internet connection</li>

    <li>🔁 ZeroTier VPN app</li>

  </ul>

  <h2>📥 Step 1: Install Required Apps</h2>

  <p><a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.ppsspp.ppsspp" class="button">Download PPSSPP (Android)</a></p>

  <p><a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.zerotier.one" class="button">Download ZeroTier (Android)</a></p>

  <h2>🎮 Step 2: Get a Multiplayer PSP Game</h2>

  <p>Use legal backups of your games or visit trusted ROM sites. Examples of supported games:</p>

  <ul>

    <li>Monster Hunter Freedom Unite</li>

    <li>God Eater Burst</li>

    <li>Dissidia 012</li>

    <li>Tekken 6</li>

  </ul>

  <p>Place the game file (.iso/.cso) in your <code>PSP > GAME</code> folder.</p>

  <h2>🌐 Step 3: Create a ZeroTier Network</h2>

  <ol>

    <li>Go to <a href="https://my.zerotier.com" target="_blank">my.zerotier.com</a></li>

    <li>Create a free account</li>

    <li>Click <strong>Create Network</strong></li>

    <li>Copy the <strong>Network ID</strong> to use later</li>

  </ol>

  <h2>📲 Step 4: Join ZeroTier Network on Android</h2>

  <ol>

